<section id="what-you-take-away">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <div class="eyebrow">What you take away</div>
    <h2 class="mt-0">One idea, and the people to test it on.</h2>
    <p>The aim is the same as the other retreats: one idea that changes how you lead &mdash; not a list of takeaways, one that holds because you worked it out somewhere real. What that idea is will be yours; the plateau is unusually good at surfacing it.</p>
    <p>You also come back with more than you left with. A few days at altitude, off the phone, generate energy and clarity out of proportion to the effort. And you will have spent four unplugged days with a small group of senior leaders from other industries &mdash; the kind of group people keep comparing notes with long after the trip.</p>
    <p>And something quieter: you will have done a hard, exposed thing you were not sure of. That has a way of resetting what counts as difficult back at the desk.</p>
  </div>
</section>

